<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR mostly unchanged, short-term lower.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR mostly unchanged, short-term lower.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were generally unchanged except for the two-week and one-month rates which were slightly weaker, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A trader said many banks were still unsure on the outlook of interest rates. Treasury bill rates have been on the ascent in the past weeks in anticipation of a possible tightness during the Christmas season.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody's waiting for the next auction, and see how rates will behave by then,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  OCT 24		 OCT 23</p>
<p>    1 W		11  3/8		 11 3/8</p>
<p>    2 W		11  5/16		11 3/8</p>
<p>    1 M		11  5/16		11 3/8</p>
<p>    2 M		11  7/16		11 7/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  9/16		11 9/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11 11/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    12M		11 13/16		11 13/16</p>
<p>    VAL		25-Oct		  24-Oct</p>
